CAT = "s66Advisers"; SEG = "ADV"
Q = [
('An accountant markets a separate stock-picking service to her tax clients for an extra fee. Under the USA she is:',
 'Investment adviser', ['Excluded as incidental advice', 'Agent of a broker-dealer', 'Exempt as a publisher'],
 'The exclusion for accountants covers advice solely incidental to the profession. Holding out an advisory service and charging for it makes her an investment adviser.'),
('Before acting in a state, a federal covered adviser makes its notice filing by giving the Administrator:',
 'Copies of its SEC filings', ['Full state registration application', 'Audited balance sheet', 'List of its clients'],
 'Under USA Section 202(b), a federal covered adviser files the documents it filed with the SEC (Form ADV) that the Administrator requires, with a notice fee and consent to service of process.'),
('An adviser solely to private funds, with under $150 million of US assets managed, is generally:',
 'Exempt reporting adviser', ['Federal covered adviser', 'Family office', 'Investment company'],
 'Advisers Act Section 203(m) exempts advisers solely to private funds with less than $150 million in US assets from SEC registration, but they still file parts of Form ADV as exempt reporting advisers.'),
('Absent any denial or proceeding, a complete state adviser registration becomes effective at:',
 'Noon on the 30th day after filing', ['Midnight on the 30th day', 'Noon on the 15th day', 'Close of business on day 10'],
 'USA Section 202(a) makes registration effective at noon of the thirtieth day after the application is filed, unless the Administrator sets an earlier date or a denial order or proceeding is pending.'),
("Under NASAA's model rule, a state adviser with discretion but no custody must keep a minimum net worth of:",
 '$10,000', ['$35,000', '$25,000', '$5,000'],
 "NASAA's minimum financial requirements rule sets $10,000 for advisers with discretionary authority and $35,000 for advisers with custody. An adviser below the minimum notifies the Administrator by the next business day."),
('A state adviser must deliver its Form ADV Part 2 brochure to a new client:',
 'Before or at contract signing', ['Within 30 days after signing', 'Only if the client asks', 'Within 48 hours after signing'],
 'The brochure rule requires delivery before or at the time of entering into the advisory contract. The old 48-hour cancellation window no longer applies.'),
('If its brochure has materially changed, an SEC adviser must give clients a summary of changes within how long after its fiscal year end?',
 '120 days', ['90 days', '60 days', '30 days'],
 'SEC Rule 204-3 requires delivery each year, within 120 days after fiscal year end, of a summary of material changes with an offer of the full brochure, or the updated brochure itself.'),
('Under Advisers Act Section 222, a state-registered adviser need only meet the books and records rules of:',
 'Its home state', ['Every state where clients live', 'The SEC', 'FINRA'],
 "Section 222 bars a state from requiring more books, records, net capital or bonding than the adviser's principal-office state requires, if the adviser complies with its home state."),
("Under NASAA's financial reporting rule, a state adviser with custody of client funds must file:",
 'Audited balance sheet', ['Unaudited income statement', 'Copy of its office lease', 'List of client balances'],
 'Advisers with custody must file an audited balance sheet each year. Advisers with only discretion file a balance sheet certified by an officer, not audited.'),
("Under SEC Rule 203A-3, a federal covered adviser's employee is an IAR if over 10% of clients are natural persons and their number exceeds:",
 'Five', ['Ten', 'Fifteen', 'Two'],
 'Rule 203A-3 defines an IAR of a federal covered adviser as a supervised person with more than five natural-person clients who also make up more than 10% of clients, not counting qualified clients.'),
('An employee of a federal covered adviser who only writes general market commentary for the public is:',
 'Not an IAR', ['IAR in every state', 'IAR where readers live', 'Agent of the adviser'],
 'Rule 203A-3 excludes supervised persons who provide only impersonal investment advice, meaning advice that does not aim to meet the needs of a specific client.'),
("Which credential generally waives the IAR exam under NASAA's model rule?",
 'CFA charter', ['Series 7 alone', 'Series 63 alone', 'Insurance producer license'],
 "NASAA's exam rule accepts the Series 65, or the Series 66 with the Series 7, or a listed designation such as CFP, ChFC, PFS, CFA or CIC. A Series 7 or 63 alone does not qualify."),
("Under NASAA's IAR continuing education program, each IAR must complete every calendar year:",
 '12 credits', ['6 credits', '24 credits', '36 credits'],
 'The model rule requires 12 credits a year: 6 in Products and Practice and 6 in Ethics and Professional Responsibility. 36 is the most a missed requirement can build up to.'),
('An IAR of a state-registered adviser applies for registration on:',
 'Form U4', ['Form ADV', 'Form BD', 'Form U5'],
 'Individuals, both IARs and agents, register through Form U4 on CRD. Form ADV registers the advisory firm, Form BD the broker-dealer, and Form U5 reports a termination.'),
('An IAR of a federal covered adviser, with an office in the state, leaves the firm. Under the USA, who must notify the Administrator?',
 'IAR', ['Federal covered adviser', 'SEC', "Each of the IAR's clients"],
 'USA Section 201(d) puts the notice on the IAR when the employer is a federal covered adviser. For a state-registered adviser, the adviser gives the notice.'),
('Under the USA, an adviser that fails to reasonably supervise its IARs may face:',
 'Revocation of registration', ['Automatic loss of all fees', 'Expulsion from FINRA', 'Prison without proof of knowledge'],
 'Failure to reasonably supervise representatives is a ground in USA Section 204 for denying, suspending or revoking registration, if the order is also in the public interest.'),
('An adviser with no office in State X advises only insurance companies there. In State X it:',
 'Need not register', ['Must register as an adviser', 'Must register all its IARs', 'Must post a surety bond'],
 'USA Section 201(c) lets an adviser with no place of business in the state skip registration when its only clients there are institutions such as insurance companies, banks and investment companies.'),
('An adviser that would otherwise register with states may register with the SEC instead if it would have to register in at least how many states?',
 '15', ['10', '5', '30'],
 'SEC Rule 203A-2 lets an adviser that would be required to register in 15 or more states register with the SEC instead.'),
('An adviser that gives all its advice through an interactive website may:',
 'Register with the SEC', ['Skip registration entirely', 'Register with FINRA only', 'Register in its home state only'],
 'SEC Rule 203A-2 has an internet adviser exemption allowing SEC registration for an adviser that advises all clients through an interactive website, subject to conditions.'),
('A mid-sized adviser registered with the SEC need not switch to state registration until its assets under management fall below:',
 '$90 million', ['$100 million', '$110 million', '$25 million'],
 'SEC Rule 203A-1 gives a buffer: an adviser may register at $100 million to $110 million, must register at $110 million, and need not withdraw until assets drop below $90 million.'),
('Under the USA, before a state-registered adviser takes custody of client funds, it must:',
 'Notify the Administrator', ["Get each client's verbal OK", 'Register as a broker-dealer', 'Join FINRA'],
 'USA Section 102(e) makes it unlawful for an adviser to have custody if it has not notified the Administrator that it has or may have custody, absent a rule.'),
('An adviser to a registered investment company, whatever its size, is:',
 'Federal covered adviser', ['State-registered adviser', 'Exempt reporting adviser', 'Excluded from the Advisers Act'],
 'Advisers to registered investment companies must register with the SEC, which makes them federal covered advisers. States can then require only notice filing.'),
('Under the Advisers Act, a family office that advises only family clients is:',
 'Excluded from the adviser definition', ['Required to register with the SEC', 'An exempt reporting adviser', 'Required to register in its state'],
 'The Dodd-Frank Act excluded family offices, as the SEC defines them, from the definition of investment adviser. They neither register nor file as exempt reporting advisers.'),
('A registered adviser forms a successor firm to take over its business. Registering the successor for the rest of the year costs:',
 'No filing fee', ['Half the usual fee', 'A full new fee', 'Double the usual fee'],
 'USA Section 202(d) lets a registered broker-dealer, federal covered adviser or investment adviser file for a successor for the unexpired part of the year, with no filing fee.'),
]
